                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7574529b-3f34-3109-8f53-f7f01540d26b",
                        "entry_id": "6cfc2510-a0b1-389a-88d0-e4f91b24b46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To temper or mix unduly; to make disproportionate; to change the due proportions of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "494b09ce-98b5-33dd-adc4-8bf4e17ac3e4",
                        "entry_id": "6cfc2510-a0b1-389a-88d0-e4f91b24b46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To derange the functions of, whether bodily, mental, or spiritual; to disorder; to disease."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8218155b-c3ff-4d7b-849f-344d68a7c6b5",
                                "sense_id": "494b09ce-98b5-33dd-adc4-8bf4e17ac3e4",
                                "text": "Guildenstern. The King, sir—\nHamlet. Ay, sir, what of him?\nGuildenstern. Is in his retirement, marvellous distemper’d.\nHamlet. With drink, sir?\nGuildenstern. No, my lord; rather with choler."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cf7928d1-bb23-41b3-8fd7-4dc7726b0af6",
                                "sense_id": "494b09ce-98b5-33dd-adc4-8bf4e17ac3e4",
                                "text": "The imagination, when completely distempered, is the most incurable of all disordered faculties."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ece626e-8229-49f2-9f27-fc3ae0faaee3",
                                "sense_id": "494b09ce-98b5-33dd-adc4-8bf4e17ac3e4",
                                "text": "To some extent the Nore Mutiny may be regarded as analogous to the distempering irruption of contagious fever in a frame constitutionally sound, and which anon throws it off."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdca8aba-0076-35ba-b2ce-7e0964823652",
                        "entry_id": "6cfc2510-a0b1-389a-88d0-e4f91b24b46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To deprive of temper or moderation; to disturb; to ruffle; to make disaffected, ill-humoured, or malignant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3b5e1126-d557-43c4-9e5c-5bdc61063672",
                                "sense_id": "bdca8aba-0076-35ba-b2ce-7e0964823652",
                                "text": "1799-1800, Samuel Taylor Coleridge (translator), The Piccolomini by Friedrich Schiller, Boston: Francis A. Niccolls & Co., 1902, p. 37,\nI have been long accustomed to defend you,\nTo heal and pacify distempered spirits."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0735f676-2b06-39bc-99db-fc75d67223e7",
                        "entry_id": "6cfc2510-a0b1-389a-88d0-e4f91b24b46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To intoxicate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "30395aa5-1662-4395-9dda-e31070e9b998",
                                "sense_id": "0735f676-2b06-39bc-99db-fc75d67223e7",
                                "text": "For the Courtiers reeling,\nAnd the Duke himselfe, (I dare not say distemperd,\nBut kind, and in his tottering chaire carousing)\nThey doe the countrie service."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a7a19cba-145d-36b4-a5fe-114ef023892f",
                        "entry_id": "6cfc2510-a0b1-389a-88d0-e4f91b24b46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To paint using distemper."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "58097ce9-f942-456b-8c80-103c051d2313",
                                "sense_id": "a7a19cba-145d-36b4-a5fe-114ef023892f",
                                "text": "He looked round the poor room, at the distempered walls, and the bad engravings in meretricious frames, the crinkly paper and wax flowers on the chiffonier; and he thought of a room like Father Bryan's, with panelling, with cut glass, with tulips in silver pots, such a room as he had hoped to have for his own."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad3065d5-6b53-463b-aaac-7b9dca582eab",
                                "sense_id": "a7a19cba-145d-36b4-a5fe-114ef023892f",
                                "text": "We cleaned out the cellars, fixed the shelves, distempered the walls, polished the woodwork, whitewashed the ceiling, stained the floor;"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "642d7a66-7767-31dd-833b-53a5b5a5b6d2",
                        "entry_id": "6cfc2510-a0b1-389a-88d0-e4f91b24b46f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To mix (colours) in the way of distemper."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e40460b4-96c1-4187-820e-3215f2a24170",
                                "sense_id": "642d7a66-7767-31dd-833b-53a5b5a5b6d2",
                                "text": "to distemper colors with size"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
